# Transient products of a running sweep.  The finished results are committed
# as .tsv.gz; these are the scratch of a run in flight.
*.err
guard.log
results/*.pid

# A sweep appends to its .tsv as it goes, so committing one while the driver is
# still running records a PARTIAL run with no way to tell from the file that it
# is partial.  That already cost this corpus one disclosed provenance defect
# (the mace4 300 s sweep has a build boundary at row 3782).  The .tsv.gz is
# written once, after the driver reports complete, and that is what is kept.
results/*.tsv
!results/*.tsv.gz

# Generated at runtime by baseline_ab.sh; not source.
.ab_one.sh
